  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: High pressure continues to build in\nacross the region, with temperatures trending warmer through\nSaturday. Slightly cooler Sunday into early next week, though\nstill above normal. \n\nRecord heat is expected in Ely this afternoon. Near record heat \nis anticipated in Elko and Eureka this afternoon. A Heat Advisory\nis in effect for most of Northern and Central Nevada from 11 AM \nPDT this morning until 9 PM PDT this evening. Record heat is \nexpected in Ely and Eureka Saturday afternoon. Near record heat is\nanticipated in Elko, Winnemucca, and Tonopah Saturday afternoon. \nRecord heat is expected in Ely and Eureka Sunday afternoon. Near \nrecord heat is anticipated in Tonopah Sunday afternoon. Heat \nAdvisories will likely be required for most of the forecast area \nSaturday and Sunday. Here are probabilities of triple digit heat \nfor select locations in Northern and Central Nevada on Saturday, \nAugust 1st, 2026: \n\nBattle Mountain - 95%\nCarlin - 95%\nElko - 90%\nWinnemucca - 90%\nWest Wendover - 90%\nWells - 90%\nSpring Creek - 85%\nTonopah - 80%\nEureka - 70%\nEly - 50%\n\nHigh temperatures throughout Northern and Central Nevada Monday\nafternoon will be around five degrees above normal for this time\nof year. Maximum temperatures across the forecast area Tuesday\nafternoon will be seven to nine degrees above seasonal values.\nHigh temperatures through Northern and Central Nevada Wednesday\nafternoon will be around ten degrees above normal for this time of\nyear. Heat Advisories may be required for parts of Northern and \nCentral Nevada Monday through Wednesday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence in \nnear record heat in most of Northern and Central Nevada each \nafternoon through Sunday. High forecast confidence regarding a \nmoderate risk of heat-related illnesses for heat-sensitive groups \neach afternoon through Sunday. High forecast confidence in above\nnormal temperatures persisting into at least the middle of next \nweek.",
